From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Attard <sam@electronjs.org>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 02:44:34 +0000
Subject: build: allow resource allowlist generation for Linux and macOS

The resource allowlist machinery (grit --allowlist-support plus
tools/resources/generate_resource_allowlist.py) works on desktop Linux via
the same linker-input scanning path Android uses, and on macOS Electron reads
the ui::AllowlistedResource<id> markers back from the linked framework's
symbol table, but the assert in gcc_toolchain.gni (which also declares the
arg that turns grit's markers on) only permits android and win.

The Linux half is https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8360559.

diff --git a/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni b/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
index ac7a5b84e93fd0bdf9eed224b2dd391621259636..78c1d0fcfd80b137d770a0064c4ffdf241f7a950 100644
--- a/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
+++ b/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
@@ -42,7 +42,8 @@ if (enable_resource_allowlist_generation) {
       !is_component_build,
       "enable_resource_allowlist_generation=true requires is_component_build=false")
   assert(
-      target_os == "android" || target_os == "win",
+      target_os == "android" || target_os == "win" || target_os == "linux" ||
+          target_os == "mac",
       "enable_resource_allowlist_generation=true does not work for target_os=$target_os")
 }
 
